      "problem": "$\\frac{2{x}^{2}-3x-4}{x-3}=$",
      "worked_solution": "We can calculate $\\frac{2{x}^{2}-3x-4}{x-3}$ using synthetic division.\n\nCarrying out the synthetic division process, we arrive at the following:\n\n|  | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $3$ | $2$ | $-3$ | $-4$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $6$ | $9$ |\n|  | $2$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2{x}^{2}-3x-4}{x-3}=2x+3+\\frac{5}{x-3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
